  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-63B Section 4.2, multi-factor authentication requires combining at least two different authentication factor types: something you know, something you have, or something you are. Two separate passwords for two different systems use the same knowledge factor category and do not constitute true MFA.
